<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rdf:RDF xmlns:cc="http://creativecommons.org/ns#" xmlns:dct="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:adms="http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#" xmlns:foaf="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/" xmlns:odrl="http://www.w3.org/ns/odrl/2/" xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#" xmlns:dcat="http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#" xmlns:lcon="http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#" xmlns:sioc="http://rdfs.org/sioc/ns#" xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xmlns:prov="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#" xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xmlns:schema="http://schema.org/" xmlns:v="http://www.w3.org/2006/vcard/ns#" xmlns:vann="http://purl.org/vocab/vann/" xmlns:voaf="http://purl.org/vocommons/voaf#" xmlns:wdrs="http://www.w3.org/2007/05/powder-s#" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#" xmlns:spdx="http://spdx.org/rdf/terms#" xmlns:time="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#" xmlns:dcatap="http://data.europa.eu/r5r/" xmlns:stat="http://data.europa.eu/s1n/statdcat-ap/" xmlns:qb="http://purl.org/linked-data/cube#" ><dcat:Dataset rdf:about="http://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/products-datasets/-/cei_srm030"><dct:issued rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2017-11-27</dct:issued><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="de">Zeitliche Frequenz</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="en">Time frequency</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="fr">Fréquence (relative au temps)</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="de">Geopolitische Meldeeinheit</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="en">Geopolitical entity (reporting)</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="fr">Entité géopolitique (déclarante)</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="de">Maßeinheit</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="en">Unit of measure</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="fr">Unité de mesure</dcat:keyword><dct:type><skos:Concept  rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/dataset-type/STATISTICAL"/></dct:type><dct:title xml:lang="en">Circular material use rate</dct:title><dct:description xml:lang="en">&lt;p&gt;The indicator measures the share of material recycled and fed back into the economy - thus saving extraction of primary raw materials - in overall material use. The circular material use, also known as circularity rate is defined as the ratio of the circular use of materials to the overall material use. The overall material use is measured by summing up the aggregate domestic material consumption (DMC) and the circular use of materials. DMC is defined in economy-wide material flow accounts. The circular use of materials is approximated by the amount of waste recycled in domestic recovery plants minus imported waste destined for recovery plus exported waste destined for recovery abroad. Waste recycled in domestic recovery plants comprises the recovery operations R2 to R11 - as defined in the Waste Framework Directive 75/442/EEC. The imports and exports of waste destined for recycling - i.e. the amount of imported and exported waste bound for recovery &amp;ndash; are approximated from the European statistics on international trade in goods. A higher circularity rate value indicates means that more secondary materials substitute for primary raw materials thus reducing the environmental impacts of extracting primary material.&lt;/p&gt;</dct:description><dct:title xml:lang="fr">Taux d&apos;utilisation circulaire de matières</dct:title><dct:description xml:lang="fr">&lt;p&gt;L&amp;rsquo;indicateur mesure la part des mati&amp;egrave;res recycl&amp;eacute;e et r&amp;eacute;introduite dans l&amp;rsquo;&amp;eacute;conomie &amp;ndash; &amp;eacute;conomisant ainsi l&amp;rsquo;extraction de mati&amp;egrave;res premi&amp;egrave;res primaires &amp;ndash; dans l&amp;rsquo;utilisation globale de mati&amp;egrave;res. Le taux d&amp;rsquo;utilisation circulaire des mati&amp;egrave;res premi&amp;egrave;res, aussi connu comme le taux de circularit&amp;eacute;, est donc d&amp;eacute;fini comme le ratio de l&amp;rsquo;utilisation circulaire des mati&amp;egrave;res premi&amp;egrave;res sur l&amp;rsquo;utilisation globale de mati&amp;egrave;res. L&amp;rsquo;utilisation globale de mati&amp;egrave;res est mesur&amp;eacute;e en additionnant l&amp;rsquo;agr&amp;eacute;gat consommation int&amp;eacute;rieure des mati&amp;egrave;res (CIM) et la quantit&amp;eacute; d&amp;rsquo;utilisation circulaire de mati&amp;egrave;res. La CIM est d&amp;eacute;finie dans les comptes des flux de mati&amp;egrave;res &amp;agrave; l&amp;rsquo;&amp;eacute;chelle de l&amp;rsquo;&amp;eacute;conomie. L&amp;rsquo;utilisation circulaire des mati&amp;egrave;res (UCM) est estim&amp;eacute;e par la quantit&amp;eacute; de d&amp;eacute;chets qui sont recycl&amp;eacute;s dans les usines nationales de r&amp;eacute;cup&amp;eacute;ration des d&amp;eacute;chets, moins les d&amp;eacute;chets import&amp;eacute;s destin&amp;eacute;s &amp;agrave; &amp;ecirc;tre r&amp;eacute;cup&amp;eacute;r&amp;eacute;s, plus les d&amp;eacute;chets export&amp;eacute;s destin&amp;eacute;s &amp;agrave; &amp;ecirc;tre r&amp;eacute;cup&amp;eacute;r&amp;eacute;s &amp;agrave; l&amp;rsquo;&amp;eacute;tranger. Les d&amp;eacute;chets recycl&amp;eacute;s dans les usines nationales de r&amp;eacute;cup&amp;eacute;ration des d&amp;eacute;chets englobent les op&amp;eacute;rations de recyclage R2 &amp;agrave; R11 &amp;ndash; telles que d&amp;eacute;finies dans la Directive relative aux d&amp;eacute;chets 75/442/CEE. Les importations et les exportations de d&amp;eacute;chets destin&amp;eacute;s au recyclage, i.e. la quantit&amp;eacute; import&amp;eacute;e et export&amp;eacute;e de d&amp;eacute;chets destin&amp;eacute;s &amp;agrave; la r&amp;eacute;cup&amp;eacute;ration, sont estim&amp;eacute;es par les Statistiques europ&amp;eacute;ennes de commerce international de marchandises. Un taux de circularit&amp;eacute; plus &amp;eacute;lev&amp;eacute; indique que davantage de mati&amp;egrave;res secondaires se substituent aux mati&amp;egrave;res premi&amp;egrave;res primaires i.e. r&amp;eacute;duisant les impacts environnementaux de l&amp;rsquo;extraction de mati&amp;egrave;res premi&amp;egrave;res.&lt;/p&gt;</dct:description><dct:title xml:lang="de">Nutzungsrate wiederverwendbarer Stoffe</dct:title><dct:description xml:lang="de">&lt;p&gt;Der Indikator misst den Anteil des recycelten und wieder in die Wirtschaft eingespeisten Materials - und spart so die Gewinnung von Prim&amp;auml;rrohstoffen - im gesamten Materialeinsatz. Die zirkul&amp;auml;re Verwendung von Materialien, auch als Zirkularit&amp;auml;tsrate bekannt ist somit definiert als das Verh&amp;auml;ltnis der zirkularen Verwendung von Materialien zu der gesamten Materialverwendung. Die Gesamtmaterialverwendung wird berechnet durch das Aggregat inl&amp;auml;ndischer Materialverbrauch (DMC) plus die Menge der zirkul&amp;auml;ren Verwendung von Materialien. DMC ist in den gesamtwirtschaftlichen Materialflussrechnungen definiert. Die zirkul&amp;auml;re Verwendung von Materialien wird durch die Menge der in inl&amp;auml;ndischen Verwertungsanlagen recycelten Abf&amp;auml;lle abz&amp;uuml;glich der zur Verwertung bestimmten importierten Abf&amp;auml;lle zuz&amp;uuml;glich der zur Verwertung im Ausland bestimmten Abf&amp;auml;lle angeglichen. Die in inl&amp;auml;ndischen Verwertungsanlagen recycelten Abf&amp;auml;lle umfassen die Verwertungsverfahren R2 bis R11 - wie in der Abfallrahmenrichtlinie 75/442 / EWG definiert. Die Importe und Exporte von Abf&amp;auml;llen, die zur Wiederverwertung bestimmt sind,-d. h die Menge der zur Verwertung bestimmten importierten und exportierten Abf&amp;auml;lle - werden durch Eurostats internationaler Wareneinkaufsstatistik gesch&amp;auml;tzt. Eine h&amp;ouml;here Zirkularit&amp;auml;tsrate zeigt an, dass mehr Sekund&amp;auml;rmaterialien prim&amp;auml;re Rohmaterialien ersetzen, d. h. die Umweltauswirkungen des Extrahierens von Prim&amp;auml;rmaterial vermeiden.&lt;/p&gt;</dct:description><dct:identifier>cei_srm030</dct:identifier><foaf:page rdf:resource="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/product/page/cei_srm030"/><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/EUR"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/BEL"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/BGR"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/CZE"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/DNK"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/DEU"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/EST"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/IRL"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/GRC"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/ESP"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/FRA"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/HRV"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/ITA"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/CYP"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/LVA"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/LTU"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/LUX"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/HUN"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/MLT"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/NLD"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/AUT"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/POL"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/PRT"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/ROU"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/SVN"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/SVK"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/FIN"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/SWE"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/ISL"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/LIE"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/NOR"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/CHE"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/GBR"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/MNE"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/MKD"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/ALB"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/SRB"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/TUR"/></dct:spatial><stat:dimension> <qb:DimensionProperty rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/sdmx/2.1/codelist/ESTAT/FREQ" > <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Zeitliche Frequenz</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Time frequency</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Fréquence (relative au temps)</skos:prefLabel> </qb:DimensionProperty> </stat:dimension><stat:dimension> <qb:DimensionProperty rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/sdmx/2.1/codelist/ESTAT/GEO" > <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Geopolitische Meldeeinheit</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Geopolitical entity (reporting)</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Entité géopolitique (déclarante)</skos:prefLabel> </qb:DimensionProperty> </stat:dimension><stat:dimension> <qb:DimensionProperty rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/sdmx/2.1/codelist/ESTAT/UNIT" > <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Maßeinheit</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Unit of measure</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Unité de mesure</skos:prefLabel> </qb:DimensionProperty> </stat:dimension><stat:attribute> <qb:AttributeProperty rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/sdmx/2.1/codelist/ESTAT/OBS_FLAG" /> </stat:attribute><stat:attribute> <qb:AttributeProperty rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/sdmx/2.1/codelist/ESTAT/CONF_STATUS" /> </stat:attribute><stat:statUnitMeasure><skos:Concept rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/sdmx/2.1/codelist/ESTAT/UNIT?code=PC"><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Prozent</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Percentage</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Pourcentage</skos:prefLabel></skos:Concept></stat:statUnitMeasure><stat:numSeries rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">28</stat:numSeries><dct:modified rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2024-11-13</dct:modified><dct:accrualPeriodicity><dct:Frequency rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/frequency/ANNUAL"/></dct:accrualPeriodicity><dct:temporal><dct:PeriodOfTime rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/PeriodOfTime/3169a64b-f3b3-4920-b709-b32c20b97678"><dcat:startDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2004-01-01</dcat:startDate><dcat:endDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2023-12-31</dcat:endDate></dct:PeriodOfTime></dct:temporal><dct:accessRights><dct:RightsStatement rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/access-right/PUBLIC"/></dct:accessRights><dcat:landingPage><foaf:Document rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/product/page/cei_srm030"><dct:type rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/documentation-type/WEBPAGE_RELATED"/><schema:url xml:lang="en">https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/product/page/cei_srm030</schema:url><dct:title xml:lang="en">More information on Eurostat Website</dct:title><dct:title xml:lang="fr">Plus d&apos;information sur le site web d&apos;Eurostat</dct:title><dct:title xml:lang="de">Mehr Informationen auf der Eurostat Website</dct:title></foaf:Document></dcat:landingPage><foaf:page><foaf:Document rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/cache/metadata/en/cei_srm030_esmsip2.htm"><dct:title xml:lang="en">ESMS metadata (Euro-SDMX Metadata structure) HTML</dct:title><foaf:topic rdf:resource="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/product/page/cei_srm030"/><schema:url xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/cache/metadata/en/cei_srm030_esmsip2.htm]]></schema:url><dct:format rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/HTML"/><dcat:mediaType rdf:resource="http://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/text/html"/><dct:type><skos:Concept rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/documentation-type/DOCUMENTATION_MAIN"/></dct:type></foaf:Document></foaf:page><foaf:page><foaf:Document rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/files?file=metadata/cei_srm030_esmsip2.sdmx.zip"><dct:title xml:lang="en">ESMS metadata (Euro-SDMX Metadata structure) SDMX</dct:title><foaf:topic rdf:resource="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/product/page/cei_srm030"/><schema:url xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/files?file=metadata/cei_srm030_esmsip2.sdmx.zip]]></schema:url><dct:format rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/XML"/><dcat:mediaType rdf:resource="http://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/application/xml"/><dct:type><skos:Concept rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/documentation-type/DOCUMENTATION_MAIN"/></dct:type></foaf:Document></foaf:page><dcat:distribution><dcat:Distribution rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/view/cei_srm030/default/table"><dct:title xml:lang="en">Table, graphs and map visualizations are also available.</dct:title><dct:title xml:lang="fr">Des visualisations sous forme de tableau, graphique et carte géographique sont aussi disponibles.</dct:title><dct:title xml:lang="de">Tabellen, Grafiken und geografische Darstellungen sind ebenfalls verfügbar.</dct:title><dcat:accessURL rdf:resource="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/view/cei_srm030/default/table"/><dct:type rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/distribution-type/VISUALIZATION"/><dct:license rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/licence/CC_BY_4_0"/><dct:rights rdf:resource="h